-soup"],["French restaurant","dish/french-restaurant"],["Fricassee","dish/fricassee"],["Garbure","dish/garbure"],["Gâteau Basque","dish/gateau-basque"],["Gugelhupf","dish/gugelhupf"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/6/6a/Daube3.JPG/500px-Daube3.JPG","w":500,"h":375,"by":"gerard cohen","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Daube3.JPG"}},"dish/dazhu-gansi":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/dazhu-gansi","n":"Dazhu gansi","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Huaiyang cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Dazhu gansi is a specialty dish of Huaiyang cuisine. Dried tofu is sliced into matchstick-sized pieces and served in chicken stock. Many other ingredients can be added to the tofu. As tofu does not have much flavor, the chef is challenged to produce knifework of great precision (a hallmark of Huaiyang cuisine) and a broth of the highest quality. It is said to have been created in Yangzhou for the Qianlong emperor."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-dazhu-gansi"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dazhu_gansi"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Huaiyang cuisine","cuisine/huaiyang-cuisine"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/e/e6/Braised_Shredded_Chicken_with_Ham_and_Dried_Tofu_2011-04.JPG/500px-Braised_Shredded_Chicken_with_Ham_and_Dried_Tofu_2011-04.JPG","w":500,"h":375,"by":"猫猫的日记本","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Braised_Shredded_Chicken_with_Ham_and_Dried_Tofu_2011-04.JPG"}},"ingredient/spinach":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/spinach","n":"Spinach","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 5 dishes across 6 cuisines","intro":[["Spinach (Spinacia oleracea) is a leafy green flowering plant native to Central and Western Asia. It is of the order Caryophyllales, family Amaranthaceae, subfamily Chenopodioideae. Its leaves are a common vegetable consumed either fresh, cooked or after storage (using preservation techniques like canning, freezing, or dehydration). The taste differs considerably between cooked and raw: the high oxalate content may be reduced by blanching."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-spinach"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spinach"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":6,"groups":[["Azerbaijani cuisine","cuisine/azerbaijani-cuisine",[["Dovga","dish/dovga"]]],["Greek cuisine","cuisine/greek-cuisine",[["Spanakorizo","dish/spanakorizo"]]],["Louisiana Creole cuisine","cuisine/louisiana-creole-cuisine",[["Eggs Sardou","dish/eggs-sardou"]]],["Trinidad and Tobago cuisine","cuisine/trinidad-and-tobago-cuisine",[["Saheena","dish/saheena"]]],["Turkish cuisine","cuisine/turkish-cuisine",[["Yayla çorbası","dish/yayla-corbas"]]],["Uzbek cuisine","cuisine/uzbek-cuisine",[["Dovga","dish/dovga"]]]]},{"h":"Where it's grown","grown":{"what":"Spinach","years":"2020 to 2024","url":"https://www.fao.org/faostat/en/#data/QCL","world":32340573,"top":[["China","cuisine/chinese-cuisine",29856854],["United States of America","cuisine/american-cuisine",359953],["Turkey","cuisine/turkish-cuisine",229971],["Japan","cuisine/japanese-cuisine",208224],["Kenya","cuisine/kenyan-cuisine",199022],["Indonesia","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",167728],["Malaysia","cuisine/malaysian-cuisine",122806],["Belgium","cuisine/belgian-cuisine",105748],["Italy","cuisine/italian-cuisine",100674],["Iran","cuisine/iranian-cuisine",99436],["France","cuisine/french-cuisine",96432],["Spain","cuisine/spanish-cuisine",88792],["Pakistan","cuisine/pakistani-cuisine",86770],["Germany","cuisine/german-cuisine",71480],["Greece","cuisine/greek-cuisine",67256]]}},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Mentha","ingredient/mentha"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Yogurt","ingredient/yogurt"],["Coriander","ingredient/coriander"],["Dill","ingredient/dill"],["Qatiq","ingredient/qatiq"],["Artichoke","ingredient/artichoke"],["Engraulis","ingredient/engraulis"],["Hollandaise sauce","ingredient/hollandaise-sauce"],["Poached egg","ingredient/poached-egg"],["Tuber","ingredient/tuber"],["Split pea","ingredient/split-pea"],["Taro","ingredient/taro"],["Feta","ingredient/feta"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/3/37/Spinacia_oleracea_Spinazie_bloeiend.jpg/500px-Spinacia_oleracea_Spinazie_bloeiend.jpg","w":500,"h":652,"by":"Rasbak","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Spinacia_oleracea_Spinazie_bloeiend.jpg"}},"ingredient/grasshopper":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/grasshopper","n":"Grasshopper","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Grasshoppers are a group of insects belonging to the suborder Caelifera. They are amongst what are possibly the most ancient living groups of chewing herbivorous insects, dating back to the early Triassic, around 250 million years ago."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-grasshopper"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grasshopper"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine",[["Inago no tsukudani","dish/inago-no-tsukudani"]]]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/b/b7/American_Bird_Grasshopper.jpg/500px-American_Bird_Grasshopper.jpg","w":500,"h":313,"by":"http://www.birdphotos.com","lic":"CC BY 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:American_Bird_Grasshopper.jpg"}},"dish/khrenovina-sauce":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/khrenovina-sauce","n":"Khrenovina sauce","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Russian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Khrenovina sauce is a spicy horseradish sauce served with a main course, popular in Siberia. It is prepared by blending fresh tomatoes, horseradish, garlic and salt. Ground black pepper, ground paprika, sweet bell pepper, vinegar, and sugar may also be added. It may be served with traditional Russian meat dishes, including pelmeni."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-khrenovina-sauce"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khrenovina_sauce"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Olga's Flavor Factory","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"olgasflavorfactory.com","note":"Russian-born home cook Olga's blog, with a dedicated Russian recipes category.","url":"https://www.olgasflavorfactory.com/category/russianrecipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Russian cuisine","links":[["Aspic","dish/aspic"],["Baba (cake)","dish/baba-cake"],["Beef Stroganoff","dish/beef-stroganoff"],["Blini","dish/blini"],["Borscht","dish/borscht"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Cabbage soup","dish/cabbage-soup"],["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["Chicken Kiev","dish/chicken-kiev"],["Chrain","dish/chrain"],["Dressed herring","dish/dressed-herring"],["Forshmak","dish/forshmak"],["Goulash","dish/goulash"],["Gugelhupf","dish/gugelhupf"],["Karelian pasty","dish/karelian-pasty"],["Kasha","dish/kasha"],["Kolach (bread)","dish/kolach-bread"],["Kringle","dish/kringle"],["Medovukha","dish/medovukha"],["Mimosa salad","dish/mimosa-salad"],["Mors (drink)","dish/mors-drink"],["Nesselrode pudding","dish/nesselrode-pudding"],["Okroshka","dish/okroshka"],["Olivier salad","dish/olivier-salad"],["Pancake","dish/pancake"],["Paska (bread)","dish/paska-bread"],["Pâté","dish/pate"],["Pelmeni","dish/pelmeni"],["Pie","dish/pie"],["Pirozhki","dish/pirozhki"],["Polonaise sauce","dish/polonaise-sauce"],["Potato pancake","dish/potato-pancake"],["Pozharsky cutlet","dish/pozharsky-cutlet"],["Rassolnik","dish/rassolnik"],["Sauerkraut","dish/sauerkraut"],["Shchi","dish/shchi"],["Solyanka","dish/solyanka"],["Sorrel soup","dish/sorrel-soup"],["Soured milk","dish/soured-milk"],["Syrniki","dish/syrniki"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/f/f1/Khrenovina-sauce.jpg/500px-Khrenovina-sauce.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"I, Leonid Dzhepko","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khrenovina-sauce.jpg"}},"ingredient/douchi":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/douchi","n":"Douchi","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Douchi, also known as doushi, shi, or tochi, is a group of fermentation-processed soybean foods most popular in the cuisine of China. The most common type of douchi, made from salted black soybeans and typically called fermented black soybeans (Chinese: 黑豆豆豉; pinyin: hēidòu dòuchǐ), Chinese fermented black beans, or salted black beans, is most widely used for making black bean sauce dishes."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-douchi"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Douchi"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine",[["Mapo tofu","dish/mapo-tofu"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Doubanjiang","ingredient/doubanjiang"],["Tofu","ingredient/tofu"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/8/89/2015_1012_Preserved_black_beans_douchi_close-up.jpg/500px-2015_1012_Preserved_black_beans_douchi_close-up.jpg","w":500,"h":500,"by":"Takeaway","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2015_1012_Preserved_black_beans_douchi_close-up.jpg"}},"ingredient/piquillo-pepper":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/piquillo-pepper","n":"Piquillo pepper","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["The piquillo pepper (pimientos del piquillo in Spanish) is a variety of chili pepper known for having a sweet taste with little to no heat. The fruits are about 7 cm long and grow productively in pots. They are traditionally grown in Northern Spain near the town of Lodosa. The name ‘piquillo’ is derived from the Spanish word for \"little beak\"."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-piquillo-pepper"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Piquillo_pepper"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Aragonese cuisine","cuisine/aragonese-cuisine",[["Regañao","dish/reganao"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Olive oil","ingredient/olive-oil"],["Sardines","ingredient/sardines"],["Serrano ham","ingredient/serrano-ham"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Yeast","ingredient/yeast"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/b/b7/Piquillo_Peppers.jpg/500px-Piquillo_Peppers.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"sindändùne -","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Piquillo_Peppers.jpg"}},"dish/spumoni":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/spumoni","n":"Spumoni","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Italian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Spumoni is a molded gelato made with layers of different colors and flavors containing candied fruits, chocolate, nuts, and nut brittle. The three main flavors are pistachio, cherry, and chocolate (or sometimes vanilla). It was created at the end of the 19th century in Naples, Italy, two hundred years after iced desserts were first made in the city. Over the following century, production of spumoni spread across southern Italy, taking on different forms by location."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-spumoni"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spumoni"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Candied fruit","ingredient/candied-fruit"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pasta Grannies","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pastagrannies.substack.com","note":"Vicky Bennison's long-running video series filming Italian grandmothers making regional pasta by hand.","url":"https://pastagrannies.substack.com/p/pasta-grannies-is-now-on-substack","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"},{"name":"Recipes from Italy","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"recipesfromitaly.com","note":"Traditional Italian recipes written by Italian home cooks, organized by region and course.","url":"https://recipesfromitaly.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Manu's Menu","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"manusmenu.com","note":"Italian-born home cook Manuela sharing classic family and regional Italian dishes.","url":"https://www.manusmenu.com/about/about-this-site","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Italian cuisine","links":[["Acquacotta","dish/acquacotta"],["Agliata","dish/agliata"],["Agnolotti","dish/agnolotti"],["Antipasto","dish/antipasto"],["Arancini","dish/arancini"],["Biscotti","dish/biscotti"],["Bolinhos de bacalhau","dish/bolinhos-de-bacalhau"],["Bombolone","dish/bombolone"],["Budino","dish/budino"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["Cannelloni","dish/cannelloni"],["Capellini","dish/capellini"],["Carbonara","dish/carbonara"],["Carpaccio","dish/carpaccio"],["Cassatella di sant'Agata","dish/cassatella-di-sant-agata"],["Cassoeula","dish/cassoeula"],["Ciabatta","dish/ciabatta"],["Cioppino","dish/cioppino"],["Coda alla vaccinara","dish/coda-alla-vaccinara"],["Colomba pasquale","dish/colomba-pasquale"],["Conti roll","dish/conti-roll"],["Cotoletta alla bolognese","dish/cotoletta-alla-bolognese"],["Crostata","dish/crostata"],["Drago restaurants","dish/drago-restaurants"],["Focaccia pugliese","dish/focaccia-pugliese"],["Frittata","dish/frittata"],["Giardiniera","dish/giardiniera"],["Guanciale","dish/guanciale"],["Italian restaurant","dish/italian-restaurant"],["Italian wedding soup","dish/italian-wedding-soup"],["Lampredotto","dish/lampredotto"],["Lasagna","dish/lasagna"],["List of Italian restaurants","dish/list-of-italian-restaurants"],["Marinara sauce","dish/marinara-sauce"],["Mondeghili","dish/mondeghili"],["Paccheri","dish/paccheri"],["Panini (sandwich)","dish/panini-sandwich"],["Panna cotta","dish/panna-cotta"],["Passatelli","dish/passatelli"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/a/a4/Spumoni_salentini.jpg/500px-Spumoni_salentini.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"i, Florixc Floriano Calcagnile","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Spumoni_salentini.jpg"}},"dish/spatzle":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/spatzle","n":"Spätzle","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 4 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Spätzle, Spätzla Knöpfle  or Spatzen, also called nokedli (Hungarian: [ˈnokɛdli]), are a type of egg pasta typically served as a side for meat dishes with sauce. Commonly associated with Swabia (hence Swabian spaetzle) and Alsace, it is also found in the cuisines of southern Germany and Austria, Switzerland, Liechtenstein, Lorraine, Moselle, Trentino and South Tyrol. It may be served as a side dish or with other ingredients like cheese and onion as a main dish. Spätzle are egg-based pasta of an irregular form with a rough, porous surface. The glutinous dough is put directly into boiling water or steam and the form varies between thin and thick, elongated and short. Spätzle is cooked for the first time during the fabrication. The moist dough is either pressed through a perforated metal plate or it drips through this plate into the boiling water. Other ways to prepare"]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-spatzle"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sp%C3%A4tzle"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Austrian cuisine","cuisine/austrian-cuisine"],["Baden cuisine","cuisine/baden-cuisine"],["Swabian cuisine","cuisine/swabian-cuisine"],["Swiss cuisine","cuisine/swiss-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Farina","ingredient/farina"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Vienna Sunday Kitchen","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"vienna-sunday.kitchen","note":"Viennese food blog of Austrian home cooking and pastries, with English-language recipes.","url":"https://www.vienna-sunday.kitchen/newest-recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Lil Vienna","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"lilvienna.com","note":"Austrian recipes from Ursula and David, two Austrians living in Boston.","url":"https://www.lilvienna.com/?p=1366","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Sabrina's Table: Swabian recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"sabrinastable.com","note":"German food blogger's collection of Swabian dishes such as Maultaschen and Spätzle.","url":"https://sabrinastable.com/en/swabian-recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Helvetic Kitchen","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"helvetickitchen.com","note":"Andie Pilot's blog of Swiss home cooking and baking, with notes on Swiss cookbooks.","url":"https://www.helvetickitchen.com/recipes/retrospective","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Austrian cuisine","links":[["Blini","dish/blini"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Chicken paprikash","dish/chicken-paprikash"],["Dampfnudel","dish/dampfnudel"],["Egg puffs and soup pearls","dish/egg-puffs-and-soup-pearls"],["Gulyásleves","dish/gulyasleves"],["Leberkäse","dish/leberkase"],["Liptauer","dish/liptauer"],["Pancake","dish/pancake"],["Potato salad","dish/potato-salad"],["Sachertorte","dish/sachertorte"],["Strudel","dish/strudel"],["Tarhonya","dish/tarhonya"],["Zopf","dish/zopf"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/a/a9/Sp%C3%A4tzle.jpg/500px-Sp%C3%A4tzle.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Qwerty Binary","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sp%C3%A4tzle.jpg"}}}